verify.overall:
I found nothing to refute. A fresh download from the official TA URL matches the claimed SHA-256 and size exactly. The file is listed with that exact URL on the P-4030DN, P-4531DN and P-5032DN pages.

All 44 claimed INF lines for the three models match byte for byte, including tab versus space, line numbers and sections. The x64 entries are under [UTAX/TA.NTamd64] and the x86 entries under [UTAX/TA.NTx86]. No entry was missed, every model is the right variant, and no hardware ID is shared by two models.

These details also check out:
- driver type: v4 XPS and OpenXPS, and PCL6 through MSxpsPCL6.dll;
- install and file sections;
- the manifests, including the P-5032DN XPS PrinterDriverID defect;
- the GPD settings (P-5032DN defaults to two-sided printing, so the code must force one-sided);
- the catalog attributes and HWID indices;
- KmInstall4.ini data;
- all four catalogs: Valid, Microsoft-signed for Windows hardware, timestamped, with every file verified, valid on Windows 10.0 and invalid on 6.2/6.3.

Only the IDs a real printer reports cannot be checked without hardware.

The other agent left out a few things that matter for the project:
- the ticket fits the driver's custom-size range;
- by the driver's own tray data, the 82.3 mm ticket can only feed from the MP tray (GPD InputBin Manual, OptionID 4);
- both packages carry the same hardware IDs, so the queue should be created with the exact driver name.

My files are under C:\Users\abdel\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\C--Users-abdel-Desktop-Amwag-Printer\7737442f-5f1d-46cc-85b0-3b47c5e9c693\scratchpad\research\kxv4-verify\, in subfolders download, extract, s (short-path copies), work (catalog JSON and certutil dumps), scripts, download-pcl5 and extract-pcl5. No printer, driver or system settings were changed.
